Why this project is GPL-3.0 rather than MIT
-------------------------------------------

The plugins in this repository are loaded into Calibre's own process and
subclass Calibre's classes directly: calibre-bridge subclasses
calibre.gui2.actions.InterfaceAction, imports calibre.ebooks.metadata,
calibre.utils.config and calibre.constants, and its configuration widget
subclasses qt.core.QWidget. Calibre is GPL-3.0 and the Qt build it bundles
is LGPL-3.0 or GPL-3.0. A plugin in that position is best treated as part
of a combined work, so this repository carries the licence that combination
requires rather than one that would advertise permissions the combination
cannot convey.

This says nothing about Bindery itself, which remains MIT. Bindery never
links Calibre: it either runs calibredb as a separate process or speaks
HTTP to this plugin, and both are arm's length interfaces.

